  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FORUM DE INVESTIMENTO DE NIASSA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Niassa Investment Forum is a follow up of the joint efforts of Niassa Government and Embassy of Ireland to promote the business potential of the province. Apart from long-term partners between Ireland and Niassa Government (26 years) partnership, in 2017, the Embassy provided support to the province to develop a new strategy plan 2018 - 2029 (PEN 2029), to replace the previous one PEP (2007-2017). The Forum aims to mobilise resources, stablish partnerships to strengthen value chains, with focus to establish business to business links in agriculture and agribusiness, oriented towards the production, processing, conservation and marketing of food crops (maize and beans) and cash crops (macadamia, soya beans and wheat).</narrative>
  </description>
